# ===== 09-quality-management.md =====
$path = Join-Path $base "09-quality-management.md"
$c = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText($path, $utf8)
$c = $c.Replace("# Quality Management`n`n", "# Quality Management`n`n> **Previous:** [Project Management](./08-project-management.md) | **Next:** [Configuration Management](./10-configuration-management.md)`n`n")
$o = "and describe approaches to continuous process improvement."
$g = "`n`n## Chapter at a Glance`n`n| Topic | Key Insight | Practical Takeaway |`n|-------|-------------|-------------------|`n| Quality Concepts | Transcendental, user, manufacturing, product, value views | ISO 25010 defines 8 quality characteristics |`n| Quality Management | QA, planning, control | Prevention is more cost-effective than detection |`n| CMMI | Five maturity levels from Initial to Optimising | Provides a roadmap for process improvement |`n| Six Sigma | DMAIC cycle for defect reduction | Target: 3.4 defects per million opportunities |`n| Reviews | Walkthroughs, technical reviews, inspections | Inspections detect 60-90% of defects |`n`n## Chapter Roadmap`n`n```mermaid`nflowchart LR`n    A[Quality Management] --> B[Quality Assurance]`n    A --> C[Quality Planning]`n    A --> D[Quality Control]`n    A --> E[ISO 9001]`n    A --> F[CMMI]`n    A --> G[Six Sigma]`n    A --> H[Reviews]`n    F --> I[Level 1-5 Maturity]`n    G --> J[DMAIC Cycle]`n    H --> K[Walkthrough Inspect Review]`n```"
$c = $c.Replace($o, $o + $g)
$c = $c.Replace("### The Concept of Software Quality`n`nSoftware quality has been defined in multiple ways", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** ISO 25010 defines quality through eight characteristics: suitability, efficiency, compatibility, usability, reliability, security, maintainability, portability.`n`n### The Concept of Software Quality`n`nSoftware quality has been defined in multiple ways")
$c = $c.Replace("### Quality Management Principles`n`nQuality management encompasses three primary activities", "> **Remember:** The prevention principle - it is 10-100x more cost-effective to prevent defects than to find and fix them after implementation.`n`n> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Quality management comprises assurance (processes), planning (standards), and control (monitoring).`n`n### Quality Management Principles`n`nQuality management encompasses three primary activities")
$c = $c.Replace("### ISO 9001`n`nISO 9001 is an international standard", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** ISO 9001 specifies QMS requirements; certification indicates defined processes, not product quality.`n`n### ISO 9001`n`nISO 9001 is an international standard")
$c = $c.Replace("### Capability Maturity Model Integration`n`nCMMI is a process improvement framework", "> **Pro Tip:** Most organisations realistically target CMMI Level 3 (Defined). Level 4-5 requires statistical process control that is difficult for creative knowledge work.`n`n> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** CMMI defines five maturity levels from ad hoc (Level 1) to quantitatively optimising (Level 5).`n`n### Capability Maturity Model Integration`n`nCMMI is a process improvement framework")
$c = $c.Replace("### Six Sigma`n`nSix Sigma is a data-driven methodology", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Six Sigmas DMAIC cycle - Define, Measure, Analyse, Improve, Control - targets 3.4 defects per million opportunities.`n`n### Six Sigma`n`nSix Sigma is a data-driven methodology")
$c = $c.Replace("### Quality Metrics`n`nQuality metrics provide quantitative data", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Key quality metrics include defect density, MTBF, and customer satisfaction scores like NPS.`n`n### Quality Metrics`n`nQuality metrics provide quantitative data")
$c = $c.Replace("### Reviews`n`nSoftware reviews are a static verification technique", "> **Pro Tip:** Fagan inspections can detect 60-90% of defects in reviewed artefacts - the most effective single quality practice available.`n`n> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Reviews range from informal walkthroughs to formal Fagan inspections with defined roles and processes.`n`n### Reviews`n`nSoftware reviews are a static verification technique")
$c = $c.Replace("### Process Improvement`n`nProcess improvement is the systematic approach", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** The IDEAL model provides five phases for process improvement: Initiating, Diagnosing, Establishing, Acting, Leveraging.`n`n### Process Improvement`n`nProcess improvement is the systematic approach")
$s = "## Summary`n`nSoftware quality management encompasses"
$r = "## Concept Comparison Table`n`n| Review Type | Formality | Roles | Defect Detection | Preparation Time |`n|-------------|-----------|-------|------------------|-----------------|`n| Walkthrough | Low | Author, attendees | Low to medium | Minimal |`n| Technical Review | Medium | Review team, author | Medium | Moderate |`n| Fagan Inspection | High | Moderator, inspectors, author, recorder | 60-90% | Significant |`n`n## Quick Reference`n`n| Concept | Definition | Example Metric |`n|---------|------------|----------------|`n| Quality Assurance | Define processes and standards | Process audit score |`n| Quality Control | Monitor conformance | Defect density |`n| Defect Density | Defects per unit size | 0.8 defects/KLOC |`n| MTBF | Mean time between failures | 720 hours |`n| DRE | Defect removal efficiency | 95% |`n| NPS | Net Promoter Score | 65 |`n`n## Cross-Application Matrix`n`n| Domain | Quality Focus | Key Standard |`n|--------|---------------|---------------|`n| Medical device | Safety, traceability | FDA, ISO 13485 |`n| Avionics | Reliability, formal verification | DO-178C |`n| Banking | Security, accuracy | PCI DSS, SOX |`n| E-commerce | Usability, performance | Internal SLAs |`n| Embedded | Reliability, efficiency | ISO 26262 |`n`n## Chapter Quiz`n`n1. How many maturity levels does CMMI define?`n   A) Three`n   B) Four`n   C) Five`n   D) Six`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**C)** CMMI defines five maturity levels: Initial, Managed, Defined, Quantitatively Managed, Optimising.</details>`n`n2. What is the Six Sigma defect target?`n   A) 3.4 defects per thousand opportunities`n   B) 3.4 defects per million opportunities`n   C) 6 defects per million opportunities`n   D) 100 defects per million opportunities`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** Six Sigma targets 3.4 defects per million opportunities, corresponding to six standard deviations.</details>`n`n3. Which review type has the highest defect detection rate?`n   A) Walkthrough`n   B) Technical review`n   C) Fagan inspection`n   D) Desk checking`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**C)** Fagan inspections can detect 60-90% of defects in inspected artefacts.</details>`n`n4. What does DMAIC stand for?`n   A) Design, Model, Analyse, Implement, Control`n   B) Define, Measure, Analyse, Improve, Control`n   C) Develop, Monitor, Assess, Improve, Correct`n   D) Define, Manage, Audit, Inspect, Certify`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** DMAIC stands for Define, Measure, Analyse, Improve, Control.</details>`n`n## Summary`n`nSoftware quality management encompasses"
$c = $c.Replace($s, $r)
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $c, $utf8)
Write-Host "OK 09-quality-management.md"

# ===== 10-configuration-management.md =====
$path = Join-Path $base "10-configuration-management.md"
$c = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText($path, $utf8)
$c = $c.Replace("# Configuration Management`n`n", "# Configuration Management`n`n> **Previous:** [Quality Management](./09-quality-management.md) | **Next:** [Agile Methodologies](./11-agile-methodologies.md)`n`n")
$o = "and explain DevOps practices."
$g = "`n`n## Chapter at a Glance`n`n| Topic | Key Insight | Practical Takeaway |`n|-------|-------------|-------------------|`n| SCM Purpose | Identify, organise, control changes | Without SCM, teams face lost work and unreliable releases |`n| Version Control | Centralised vs distributed | Git dominates with lightweight branching |`n| Change Management | Submit, analyse, approve, implement | CCB reviews changes for impact |`n| CI/CD | Automate integration to deployment | CI builds and tests; CD delivers to production |`n| DevOps | Dev and Ops collaboration | Three ways: flow, feedback, learning |`n`n## Chapter Roadmap`n`n```mermaid`nflowchart LR`n    A[SCM] --> B[Version Control]`n    A --> C[Change Management]`n    A --> D[Build Management]`n    A --> E[Release Management]`n    A --> F[CI/CD]`n    A --> G[DevOps]`n    B --> H[Git Centralised Distributed]`n    F --> I[Continuous Integration]`n    F --> J[Continuous Delivery]`n    G --> K[IaC Automation]`n```"
$c = $c.Replace($o, $o + $g)
$c = $c.Replace("### The Purpose of Configuration Management`n`nSoftware configuration management (SCM) is the discipline", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** SCM ensures correct artefact versions are used and changes are controlled throughout the software lifecycle.`n`n### The Purpose of Configuration Management`n`nSoftware configuration management (SCM) is the discipline")
$c = $c.Replace("### Version Control`n`nVersion control is the foundation", "> **Pro Tip:** Git feature branch workflow with pull requests provides code review, CI triggers, and clean history - the industry standard for team development.`n`n> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Git dominates version control with lightweight branching and distributed architecture supporting offline work.`n`n### Version Control`n`nVersion control is the foundation")
$c = $c.Replace("### Change Management`n`nChange management controls how changes", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** The change control board evaluates change requests through impact analysis on cost, schedule, and quality.`n`n### Change Management`n`nChange management controls how changes")
$c = $c.Replace("### Build Management`n`nBuild management automates the process", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Build tools automate compilation, dependency resolution, testing, and packaging; reproducible builds are the gold standard.`n`n### Build Management`n`nBuild management automates the process")
$c = $c.Replace("### Release Management`n`nRelease management controls the process", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Semantic versioning (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH) communicates change impact through the version number.`n`n### Release Management`n`nRelease management controls the process")
$c = $c.Replace("### Continuous Integration`n`nContinuous integration (CI) is the practice", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** CI merges changes frequently, builds and tests each integration, and gives immediate feedback on quality.`n`n### Continuous Integration`n`nContinuous integration (CI) is the practice")
$c = $c.Replace("### Continuous Delivery`n`nContinuous delivery (CD) extends CI", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** CD ensures every change passing CI can be released to production; continuous deployment automates the final step.`n`n### Continuous Delivery`n`nContinuous delivery (CD) extends CI")
$c = $c.Replace("### DevOps Practices`n`nDevOps is a cultural and professional movement", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** DevOps emphasises IaC, automated deployment, monitoring, blameless culture, and rapid feedback from production.`n`n### DevOps Practices`n`nDevOps is a cultural and professional movement")
$c = $c.Replace("### Infrastructure as Code`n`nInfrastructure as code (IaC) treats infrastructure", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Configuration management tools (Ansible, Chef) configure servers; provisioning tools (Terraform, CloudFormation) create infrastructure.`n`n### Infrastructure as Code`n`nInfrastructure as code (IaC) treats infrastructure")
$s = "## Summary`n`nConfiguration management controls"
$r = "## Concept Comparison Table`n`n| Tool Category | Examples | Purpose | Declarative? | Agent Required? |`n|--------------|----------|---------|--------------|----------------|`n| Version Control | Git, SVN, Mercurial | Track file changes | N/A | No (DVCS local) |`n| Build Automation | Maven, Gradle, Make | Compile and package | Partial | No |`n| CI/CD | Jenkins, GitLab CI, GitHub Actions | Automate pipeline | Yes | Yes (runner) |`n| Provisioning | Terraform, CloudFormation | Create infrastructure | Yes | No |`n| Config Mgmt | Ansible, Chef, Puppet | Configure servers | Yes | Varies |`n| Containerisation | Docker, Kubernetes | Package and orchestrate | Yes | Yes (K8s agent) |`n`n## Quick Reference`n`n| Concept | Definition | Key Benefit |`n|---------|------------|-------------|`n| SCM | Control artefact changes | Reliability and traceability |`n| CI | Frequent integration with automated build | Early defect detection |`n| CD | Automated delivery to production | Faster, safer releases |`n| IaC | Infrastructure managed as code | Repeatable, version-controlled |`n| Semantic Versioning | MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH | Communicates change impact |`n| Gitflow | Branching model for enterprise | Clear separation of concerns |`n`n## Cross-Application Matrix`n`n| Team Size | Recommended VCS Workflow | CI/CD Complexity |`n|-----------|--------------------------|------------------|`n| 1-3 developers | Centralised or feature branch | Simple CI only |`n| 4-10 developers | Feature branch with PRs | Full CI/CD pipeline |`n| 10-50 developers | Gitflow or trunk-based | Multi-stage pipeline |`n| 50+ developers | Trunk-based with feature flags | Sophisticated with canary |`n`n## Chapter Quiz`n`n1. Which semantic version component is incremented for incompatible API changes?`n   A) PATCH`n   B) MINOR`n   C) MAJOR`n   D) BUILD`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**C)** MAJOR version is incremented for incompatible API changes.</details>`n`n2. What distinguishes continuous delivery from continuous deployment?`n   A) CDelivery requires manual approval to deploy; CDeployment automates it`n   B) CDeployment runs more tests`n   C) CDelivery is for web apps only`n   D) There is no difference`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**A)** Continuous delivery keeps software deployable but requires manual approval; continuous deployment automates the production release.</details>`n`n3. Which tool is primarily a provisioning tool (creates infrastructure)?`n   A) Ansible`n   B) Chef`n   C) Terraform`n   D) Puppet`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**C)** Terraform provisions infrastructure resources; Ansible, Chef, and Puppet configure existing servers.</details>`n`n4. What are the three ways of DevOps?`n   A) Plan, Build, Run`n   B) Flow, Feedback, Continuous Learning`n   C) Dev, Test, Ops`n   D) Code, Build, Deploy`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** Gene Kims three ways: flow (accelerate delivery), feedback (amplify info back), and continuous learning (experimentation).</details>`n`n## Summary`n`nConfiguration management controls"
$c = $c.Replace($s, $r)
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $c, $utf8)
Write-Host "OK 10-configuration-management.md"

# ===== 11-agile-methodologies.md =====
$path = Join-Path $base "11-agile-methodologies.md"
$c = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText($path, $utf8)
$c = $c.Replace("# Agile Methodologies`n`n", "# Agile Methodologies`n`n> **Previous:** [Configuration Management](./10-configuration-management.md) | **Next:** [DevOps and CI/CD](./12-devops-cicd.md)`n`n")
$o = "and describe agile testing practices and their integration with development."
$g = "`n`n## Chapter at a Glance`n`n| Topic | Key Insight | Practical Takeaway |`n|-------|-------------|-------------------|`n| Scrum | Roles (PO, SM, Dev), events, artefacts | Lightweight framework for complex work |`n| Kanban | Visualise work, limit WIP, manage flow | Best for unpredictable, continuous flow work |`n| Scrum vs Kanban | Iterations vs flow, prescribed vs flexible | Choose by context: product dev vs support |`n| Scaled Agile | SAFe (structured) vs LeSS (minimalist) | Scaling adds coordination overhead |`n| Agile Estimation | Story points, planning poker, velocity | Relative sizing works better than absolute |`n`n## Chapter Roadmap`n`n```mermaid`nflowchart LR`n    A[Agile Methodologies] --> B[Scrum]`n    A --> C[Kanban]`n    A --> D[Scaled Frameworks]`n    A --> E[Agile Estimation]`n    A --> F[Agile Testing]`n    B --> G[Roles Product Owner SM Dev]`n    B --> H[Events Sprint Daily Review Retro]`n    B --> I[Artefacts Backlog Increment]`n    C --> J[WIP Limits Flow]`n    D --> K[SAFe LeSS]`n```"
$c = $c.Replace($o, $o + $g)
$c = $c.Replace("### Agile Fundamentals`n`nAgile methodologies are founded", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Agile methodologies translate manifesto values into concrete practices - iterative, incremental, collaborative.`n`n### Agile Fundamentals`n`nAgile methodologies are founded")
$c = $c.Replace("### Scrum`n`nScrum is a lightweight framework", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Scrum provides minimal structure - three roles, five events, three artefacts - built on transparency, inspection, adaptation.`n`n### Scrum`n`nScrum is a lightweight framework")
$c = $c.Replace("### Kanban`n`nKanban is an agile method", "> **Pro Tip:** Start Kanban with your existing process, visualise it on a board, add WIP limits, then evolve. Incremental change without disruption.`n`n> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Kanban emphasises visualising workflow, limiting WIP, managing flow, and continuous improvement.`n`n### Kanban`n`nKanban is an agile method")
$c = $c.Replace("### Scrum versus Kanban`n`nScrum and Kanban differ in several", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Scrum suits product development with iterations; Kanban suits support work with continuous flow and variable priority.`n`n### Scrum versus Kanban`n`nScrum and Kanban differ in several")
$c = $c.Replace("### Scaled Agile Frameworks`n`nWhen agile methods are applied", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** SAFe uses Agile Release Trains and Program Increments; LeSS keeps Scrum minimal across multiple teams.`n`n### Scaled Agile Frameworks`n`nWhen agile methods are applied")
$c = $c.Replace("### Agile Estimation`n`nAgile estimation techniques acknowledge", "> **Remember:** Velocity is team-specific - never compare velocity across different teams or use it for performance evaluation.`n`n> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Story points provide relative sizing; planning poker builds consensus; velocity guides future Sprint planning.`n`n### Agile Estimation`n`nAgile estimation techniques acknowledge")
$c = $c.Replace("### Agile Testing`n`nAgile testing integrates testing", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** The agile testing quadrants classify tests by technology vs business-facing and support vs critique purposes.`n`n### Agile Testing`n`nAgile testing integrates testing")
$s = "## Summary`n`nAgile methodologies translate"
$r = "## Concept Comparison Table`n`n| Aspect | Scrum | Kanban |`n|--------|-------|--------|`n| Cadence | Fixed iterations (Sprints) | Continuous flow |`n| Work Limit | Sprint scope (commitment) | WIP limits per column |`n| Roles | PO, SM, Dev Team | None prescribed |`n| Changes during iteration | Not allowed | Allowed if capacity permits |`n| Metrics | Velocity | Lead time, cycle time, throughput |`n| Best For | Product development | Support, maintenance, Ops |`n`n## Quick Reference`n`n| Concept | Definition | Key Metric |`n|---------|------------|-------------|`n| Sprint | Time-boxed iteration (1 month or less) | Sprint Goal |`n| Product Backlog | Ordered list of everything needed | Prioritisation |`n| Sprint Backlog | Items selected for Sprint + plan | Real-time work view |`n| Increment | Sum of all completed items | Definition of Done |`n| Story Points | Relative effort unit | Velocity |`n| Lead Time | Request to delivery | Total flow time |`n| Cycle Time | Work started to delivered | Processing time |`n`n## Cross-Application Matrix`n`n| Context | Recommended Approach | Key Practice |`n|---------|----------------------|---------------|`n| New product development | Scrum | Sprint reviews with stakeholders |`n| IT support team | Kanban | WIP limits, prioritise by urgency |`n| Multi-team programme | SAFe | ART, PI planning |`n| Small co-located team | LeSS | One backlog, one PO |`n| Maintenance + features | Scrumban | Sprint cadence + Kanban flow |`n`n## Chapter Quiz`n`n1. What are the three roles in Scrum?`n   A) Manager, Developer, Tester`n   B) Product Owner, Scrum Master, Development Team`n   C) Product Manager, Tech Lead, QA`n   D) Owner, Coach, Contributor`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** Scrum defines three roles: Product Owner, Scrum Master, and Development Team.</details>`n`n2. What is the maximum time-box for a Daily Scrum?`n   A) 5 minutes`n   B) 15 minutes`n   C) 30 minutes`n   D) 1 hour`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** The Daily Scrum is time-boxed to 15 minutes for synchronisation.</details>`n`n3. Which Kanban metric measures total time from request to delivery?`n   A) Cycle time`n   B) Lead time`n   C) Throughput`n   D) Velocity`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** Lead time measures the total time from a work item being requested to its delivery.</details>`n`n4. What does SAFe call a team-of-teams delivering value in a Program Increment?`n   A) Scrum Team`n   B) Agile Release Train`n   C) Product Group`n   D) Squad`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** SAFe organises teams into Agile Release Trains (ARTs) that deliver in Program Increments of 8-12 weeks.</details>`n`n## Summary`n`nAgile methodologies translate"
$c = $c.Replace($s, $r)
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $c, $utf8)
Write-Host "OK 11-agile-methodologies.md"

# ===== 12-devops-cicd.md =====
$path = Join-Path $base "12-devops-cicd.md"
$c = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText($path, $utf8)
$c = $c.Replace("# DevOps and CI/CD`n`n", "# DevOps and CI/CD`n`n> **Previous:** [Agile Methodologies](./11-agile-methodologies.md) | **Next:** [Security Engineering](./13-security-engineering.md)`n`n")
$o = "and compare deployment strategies including blue-green, canary, and rolling deployments."
$g = "`n`n## Chapter at a Glance`n`n| Topic | Key Insight | Practical Takeaway |`n|-------|-------------|-------------------|`n| DevOps Culture | Dev + Ops collaboration | Three ways: flow, feedback, learning |`n| CI/CD Pipelines | Automate commit to deploy | Jenkins, GitLab CI, GitHub Actions |`n| Infrastructure as Code | Terraform provision, Ansible configure | Repeatable, version-controlled infra |`n| Containerisation | Docker package, K8s orchestrate | Consistent across environments |`n| Deployment Strategies | Rolling, blue-green, canary | Canary provides highest safety |`n`n## Chapter Roadmap`n`n```mermaid`nflowchart LR`n    A[DevOps] --> B[CI/CD Pipelines]`n    A --> C[IaC]`n    A --> D[Containerisation]`n    A --> E[Monitoring]`n    A --> F[Deployment Strategies]`n    B --> G[Jenkins GitLab GitHub Actions]`n    C --> H[Terraform Ansible]`n    D --> I[Docker Kubernetes]`n    F --> J[Rolling Blue-Green Canary]`n```"
$c = $c.Replace($o, $o + $g)
$c = $c.Replace("### The DevOps Culture`n`nDevOps represents the convergence", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** DevOps unifies Dev and Ops through collaboration, automation, measurement, and a blameless culture.`n`n### The DevOps Culture`n`nDevOps represents the convergence")
$c = $c.Replace("### CI/CD Pipelines`n`nContinuous integration and continuous delivery pipelines", "> **Pro Tip:** Keep pipeline stages fast - developers need feedback within minutes, not hours. Parallelise long-running stages.`n`n> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** A CI/CD pipeline automates source, build, test, analyse, package, stage, and deploy stages.`n`n### CI/CD Pipelines`n`nContinuous integration and continuous delivery pipelines")
$c = $c.Replace("### Infrastructure as Code`n`nInfrastructure as code (IaC) applies", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Terraform provisions infrastructure declaratively; Ansible configures software on existing servers agentlessly.`n`n### Infrastructure as Code`n`nInfrastructure as code (IaC) applies")
$c = $c.Replace("### Containerisation`n`nContainerisation packages software", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Docker packages apps with dependencies; Kubernetes orchestrates containers at scale with self-healing and rolling updates.`n`n### Containerisation`n`nContainerisation packages software")
$c = $c.Replace("### Monitoring and Logging`n`nMonitoring provides visibility", "> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Observability rests on three pillars: metrics (Prometheus), logs (Elastic Stack), and traces (OpenTelemetry).`n`n### Monitoring and Logging`n`nMonitoring provides visibility")
$c = $c.Replace("### Deployment Strategies`n`nThe deployment strategy determines", "> **Warning:** Blue-green requires double infrastructure; canary needs sophisticated traffic routing. Start with rolling if you have limited operational maturity.`n`n> **One-Sentence Takeaway:** Rolling updates gradually; blue-green switches environments; canary tests on small traffic before full rollout.`n`n### Deployment Strategies`n`nThe deployment strategy determines")
$s = "## Summary`n`nDevOps unifies development"
$r = "## Concept Comparison Table`n`n| Deployment Strategy | Rollback Speed | Infrastructure Cost | Traffic Control | Safety |`n|--------------------|----------------|---------------------|-----------------|--------|`n| Rolling | Slow | Low | None needed | Medium |`n| Blue-Green | Instant | Double | Switch | High |`n| Canary | Instant | Single + canary | % based routing | Highest |`n`n## Quick Reference`n`n| Concept | Tool | Purpose |`n|---------|------|---------|`n| CI/CD Pipeline | Jenkins, GitLab CI, GitHub Actions | Automate build-test-deploy |`n| IaC Provisioning | Terraform | Create cloud resources |`n| Config Management | Ansible | Configure server software |`n| Container Runtime | Docker | Package and run containers |`n| Orchestration | Kubernetes | Manage container clusters |`n| Metrics | Prometheus + Grafana | Collect and visualise |`n| Logs | Elasticsearch + Kibana | Centralised logging |`n| Traces | OpenTelemetry | Distributed tracing |`n`n## Cross-Application Matrix`n`n| System Type | CI/CD Tool | Deployment Strategy | IaC Approach |`n|-------------|-----------|---------------------|--------------|`n| Web application | GitHub Actions | Rolling or blue-green | Terraform + Ansible |`n| Microservices | GitLab CI | Canary | Terraform + K8s |`n| Mobile app | Jenkins | Phased rollout | N/A |`n| Embedded firmware | Custom | Rolling | N/A |`n| Data pipeline | Airflow + CI | Blue-green | Terraform |`n`n## Chapter Quiz`n`n1. What are the three ways of DevOps?`n   A) Plan, Code, Deploy`n   B) Flow, Feedback, Continuous Learning`n   C) Build, Test, Release`n   D) Design, Implement, Monitor`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** The three ways: flow (accelerate delivery), feedback (amplify info), and continuous learning (experimentation).</details>`n`n2. Which deployment strategy provides the fastest rollback?`n   A) Rolling`n   B) Blue-green`n   C) Canary`n   D) Recreate`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** Blue-green switches traffic instantly between environments - fastest rollback.</details>`n`n3. What does a readiness probe check in Kubernetes?`n   A) Whether the pod is alive`n   B) Whether the pod is ready to serve traffic`n   C) CPU utilisation`n   D) Memory usage`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**B)** A readiness probe determines whether a pod is ready to accept traffic; it controls service endpoint membership.</details>`n`n4. Which tool is agentless and connects via SSH?`n   A) Chef`n   B) Puppet`n   C) Ansible`n   D) SaltStack`n`n<details><summary>Answer</summary>**C)** Ansible is agentless - it connects to managed nodes via SSH and executes modules.</details>`n`n## Summary`n`nDevOps unifies development"
$c = $c.Replace($s, $r)
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $c, $utf8)
Write-Host "OK 12-devops-cicd.md"

